          "path": "_m/g/c/k/8/cardigan-castle-wp/knight-at-the-castle-geograph-.jpg",
          "filename": "Knight at the castle - geograph.org.uk - 508505.jpg",
          "caption": "Knight at the castle This giant dummy, although about 15 feet tall, is dwarfed by the huge trees which have grown up over the years since they were originally planted in the grounds of Castle Green House, built in the keep in 1827. It is likely that specimen trees and shrubs were cultivated and some have continued to thrive unchecked. Recently several unusual varieties of holly were identified here.",
